  "equipment_type": "Battery charger (industrial float charger, UPS-type DC system)",
  "applies_to": "HindlePower AT10.1 and AT30 microprocessor-controlled float battery chargers fitted with the AT Series Communications Module (EJ5037-##) set to Modbus, per operating instructions JA0102-04 Rev. 02-2025.",
  "summary": "HindlePower's AT10.1 and AT30 industrial float battery chargers can carry a communications module that speaks Modbus RTU or ASCII (or DNP3) over RS-232/RS-485, with optional Ethernet. Charger modes are coils, alarms are discrete inputs, measurements are input registers and setpoints are holding registers, all 16-bit with a fixed multiplier. This map covers the full published Modbus register set.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "ASCII",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Registers are printed with Modicon prefixes (00001 coils, 10001 discrete inputs, 30001 input registers, 40001 holding registers) and the implementation follows the Modicon PI-MBUS-300 guide, so 30001 is input register 0 on the wire, 40001 holding register 0, and so on."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "Charger main control board software Rev. 3.00 or higher",
  "source": {
    "title": "AT10.1/AT30 Series Microprocessor-Controlled Float Battery Charger - Communications Module (DNP3 Level 2 / Modbus Protocols) Operating Instructions",
    "doc_number": "JA0102-04 Rev. 02-2025",
    "revision_date": "2025-02",
    "url": "https://www.hindlepowerinc.com/media/j5mfmli1/ja0102-04.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 2 (serial settings), pp. 14-16 printed (PDF pp. 16-18: DIP switches, setup program, Modbus TCP port), pp. 30-32 (Modbus function codes, register definitions, multipliers, scaling sample), p. 33 (data ranges)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Scaling: each register has a multiplier; the raw value is divided by it (manual's example: 30006 = 1300 means 130.0 V). Scale = 1 / multiplier.",
    "Left out: 30010 Battery temperature (°C, multiplier 1): the manual does not say whether below-zero temperatures are sent as signed values.",
    "Modbus RTU settings: 8 data bits with none/even/odd parity (1 or 2 stop bits with no parity); ASCII uses 7 data bits. Baud is 9600 or 19200 (DIP S1-7). The Modbus address is set in binary on DIP S2. The setup program's factory defaults are no parity and 1 stop bit.",
    "Modbus over TCP/IP is available with the Ethernet option; it is disabled by default (setup program item 'Enable Modbus over TCP/IP') and its default port is 502. Port 20000 is the default for DNP3 over TCP, not Modbus.",
    "Only one equalize method coil can be active; switching one on turns the other two off, and the method cannot be switched off."
  ],
